; Teller, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.c9c54dbd45c61015d10658ba8eddaa9270117297.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.c9c54dbd45c61015d10658ba8eddaa9270117297.001.1"},{"event":"Special Weather Statement","headline":"Special Weather Statement issued August 26 at 3:52PM MDT by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"At 352 PM MDT, Doppler radar was tracking a strong thunderstorm near\nStonewall, or 24 miles west of Trinidad, moving southeast at 25 mph.\n\nHAZARD...Wind gusts up to 50 mph and half inch hail.\n\nSOURCE...Radar indicated.\n\nIMPACT...Gusty winds could knock down tree limbs and blow around\nunsecured objects. Minor hail damage to vegetation is\npossible.\n\nLocations impacted include...\nStonewall, Segundo, Raton Pass, and Weston.","ends":"2026-08-26T16:45:00-06:00","severity":"Moderate","areaDesc":"Southern Sangre De Cristo Mountains Between 7500 and 11000 Ft; Trinidad Vicinity/Western Las Animas County Below 7500 Ft","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.47d32a55db27d6dd6bd52661f3910933b0add49b.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.47d32a55db27d6dd6bd52661f3910933b0add49b.001.1"},{"event":"Flash Flood Watch","headline":"Flash Flood Watch issued August 26 at 12:32PM MDT until August 26 at 9:00PM MDT by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"* WHAT...Flash flooding and debris flows caused by excessive rainfall\nwill be possible over the Aspen Acres Burn Scar.\n\n* WHERE...Aspen Acres Burn Scar.\n\n* WHEN...Until 9 PM MDT this evening.\n\n* IMPACTS...Heavy rainfall over the Aspen Acres Burn Scar is expected\nup to and during the period of the watch. Residents near the Aspen\nAcres Burn Scar should prepare for debris flows and stay up to date\nwith information from local authorities. Heavy rainfall could\ntrigger flash flooding of low-lying areas and debris flows in and\nnear recent wildfire burn scars.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- National Weather Service Meteorologists are forecasting heavy\nrainfall over the burn scar, which may lead to flash flooding and\ndebris flows.\n- Some locations that may experience flash flooding include...\nBeulah, San Isabel and Highways 165 and 78 in and around the\nAspen Acres Burn Scar.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-08-26T21:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Wet Mountains between 6300 and 10000Ft; Wet Mountains above 10000 Ft; Pueblo Vicinity/Pueblo County Below 6300 Feet","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.9ff2c4a7c1a7690fe1b763a7ff251163efdc6a00.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.9ff2c4a7c1a7690fe1b763a7ff251163efdc6a00.001.1"},{"event":"Flash Flood Watch","headline":"Flash Flood Watch issued August 26 at 12:32PM MDT until August 27 at 9:00PM MDT by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"* WHAT...Flash flooding and debris flows caused by excessive rainfall\nwill be possible over the Aspen Acres Burn Scar.\n\n* WHERE...Aspen Acres Burn Scar.\n\n* WHEN...Until 9 PM MDT this evening.\n\n* IMPACTS...Heavy rainfall over the Aspen Acres Burn Scar is expected\nup to and during the period of the watch. Residents near the Aspen\nAcres Burn Scar should prepare for debris flows and stay up to date\nwith information from local authorities. Heavy rainfall could\ntrigger flash flooding of low-lying areas and debris flows in and\nnear recent wildfire burn scars.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- National Weather Service Meteorologists are forecasting heavy\nrainfall over the burn scar, which may lead to flash flooding and\ndebris flows.\n- Some locations that may experience flash flooding include...\nBeulah, San Isabel and Highways 165 and 78 in and around the\nAspen Acres Burn Scar.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-08-27T21:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Wet Mountains between 6300 and 10000Ft; Wet Mountains above 10000 Ft; Pueblo Vicinity/Pueblo County Below 6300 Feet","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.9ff2c4a7c1a7690fe1b763a7ff251163efdc6a00.001.2","url":"https://api.weather.gov/aler